---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { COUNTRIES, DATA_VERSION } from '../lib/vat';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Us — VatSnap, Free Unofficial EU VAT Tool"
  description="About VatSnap: a free, unofficial EU VAT rate calculator for small online sellers. Rates track the European Commission TEDB."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <h1>About Us</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    VatSnap is a free, unofficial VAT rate calculator built for small online
    sellers — Etsy, Shopify, Amazon and independent shops selling into the EU.
  </p>
  <div class="card">
    <h2>Why we built this</h2>
    <p>
      EU VAT rates live scattered across official tables that are hard to use
      at checkout speed. We wanted one fast page per country — standard rate,
      reduced rates, and a calculator preset to that country — covering all 27
      EU members plus the UK for reference ({COUNTRIES.length} pages total).
    </p>
    <h2>Where the numbers come from</h2>
    <p>
      Every rate on this site is bundled at build time from open data tracking
      the European Commission's Taxes in Europe Database (TEDB). No rate is ever
      typed by hand into the UI — the calculator reads the dataset directly, so
      updates flow straight through on the next build.
      Rates shown were last verified {DATA_VERSION}.
    </p>
    <h2>Important disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      VatSnap is a guidance tool, not tax advice. VAT treatment depends on
      place of supply, customer status, product category, thresholds and
      exemptions that this calculator cannot know. Always confirm rates and
      filing obligations with a qualified accountant or the official EU TEDB
      source before invoicing or filing. See our <a href="/terms/">Terms</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Cost &amp; privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The site is fully static — no backend, no database, no accounts, no
      tracking. Calculations happen in your browser. Read the full
      <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Found an error or want a feature? Head to our
      <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> — rate corrections with an official
      source link are especially welcome.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
